		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=413#comment-24155</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[My heart was touched, broken, and enriched by Srimati more than any words could say. From among so many memories from the brief week I spent with her in the summer of 2007, I will share this: In one of her afternoon raga classes at Southwest Sufi Camp, we witnessed her demonstration of mastery of raga as she manipulated the rain falling around the farmhouse by singing her taans, twice within the span of about one minute I will never forget. A true master does not die. ? ?????? ?????? ???????
OM Shanti, Shanti, Shantihee]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>My heart was touched, broken, and enriched by Srimati more than any words could say. From among so many memories from the brief week I spent with her in the summer of 2007, I will share this: In one of her afternoon raga classes at Southwest Sufi Camp, we witnessed her demonstration of mastery of raga as she manipulated the rain falling around the farmhouse by singing her taans, twice within the span of about one minute I will never forget. A true master does not die. ? ?????? ?????? ???????<br />
OM Shanti, Shanti, Shantihee</p>
]]></content:encoded>
